From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: charge NPU RX drops to the poll budget

NPU dequeue returns NULL both when no complete packet is available and
when it consumed malformed descriptors or failed to build an skb. In the
latter case, completing NAPI immediately leaves already completed packets
behind the drop waiting for another interrupt.

Check queue progress around dequeue. Charge a consumed drop as one packet
of NAPI work and continue polling within the budget. A NULL result with
no progress still stops the poll, including partial hardware completions.
Keep the existing zero-budget page-pool guard.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
--- a/npu.c
+++ b/npu.c
@@ -220,6 +220,7 @@
 {
 	struct mt76_dev *dev = mt76_priv(napi->dev);
 	enum mt76_rxq_id qid = napi - dev->napi;
+	struct mt76_queue *q = &dev->q_rx[qid];
 	struct airoha_npu *npu;
 	int done = 0;
 
@@ -234,18 +235,27 @@
 
 	while (done < budget) {
 		struct sk_buff *skb;
+		int queued = q->queued;
 		u32 info = 0;
 
-		skb = mt76_npu_dequeue(dev, &dev->q_rx[qid], &info);
-		if (!skb)
-			break;
+		skb = mt76_npu_dequeue(dev, q, &info);
+		if (!skb) {
+			if (q->queued == queued)
+				break;
+
+			/* A dropped packet consumed descriptors. Keep polling the
+			 * completed packets behind it, but account for the work.
+			 */
+			done++;
+			continue;
+		}
 
 		dev->drv->rx_skb(dev, qid, skb, &info);
 		mt76_rx_poll_complete(dev, qid, napi);
 		done++;
 	}
 
-	mt76_npu_fill_rx_queue(dev, &dev->q_rx[qid]);
+	mt76_npu_fill_rx_queue(dev, q);
 out:
 	if (done < budget && napi_complete(napi))
 		dev->drv->rx_poll_complete(dev, qid);
